{"span": 106.5, "stage": "finalize_pair.s_base", "allclose_failures": 1, "total_elements": 524288, "points_truncated": false, "points": [{"index": [0, 31, 54, 126], "native": 130.0, "cpu_fp32_seam": 50.25, "absolute_difference": 79.75, "allclose_allowance": 50.251, "bf16_bit_distance": 185}], "rule_unchanged": {"mode": "allclose", "rtol": 1.0, "atol": 0.001, "max_relative_l2": 1e-05, "reason": "finalize_pair's four products are FP32 dot products over 64 terms whose operands still carry the un-cancelled pairwise decay: measured on a 910B3, the operands span 13 decades (|k_scaled| up to 1.8e+13) and the sums reach 3.3e+08, so the terms cancel catastrophically. The device and torch sum in different orders, so elements near a cancellation disagree by tens of BF16 ulp while the vector norm does not. Measured over four cases (C=1,2,3 and HV=1,2,4): the worst elementwise disagreement is 58 ulp, at most 0.41% of elements exceed 1 ulp, and the worst relative L2 is 1.06e-07 (qk_right; s_base 1.1e-11, t_beta 1.6e-10, qk_left 2.9e-09). The relative L2 bound of 1e-5 is therefore the real criterion here, two orders above the worst measurement; the elementwise rtol of 1.0 is kept only as a gross-error guard, about twice the worst observed relative deviation (58 ulp is 0.23 to 0.45 of the value). These checkpoints are only meaningful once multiplied by the matching row or column scale, which finalize_post does. The budget was set after seeing device results; the six outputs keep the a5.kda_bwd budgets unchanged, and finalize_pre's scalings needed no relaxation at all (0 ulp, relative L2 at most 3.7e-27)."}, "source_tensor_sha256": "2925ad0583e39935f6d76b1835431f0ee955bce7237fe6bdae5b0c7c96c5778b", "fp64_is_not_acceptance_golden": true}
